benchmarks/subset/ulr_vs_upl -- the 100 programs of [2] ULR vs UPL for --subset
==================================================================================

Drawn uniformly at random, with a fixed seed, from the 1,087 programs of benchmarks/ulr_vs_upl
(Figure 6): 96 of its 1,048 C programs and 4 of its 39 Boogie programs, its proportions. In
Python 3:

    rng = random.Random(2027)
    c   = rng.sample(sorted(c_programs), 96)
    bpl = rng.sample(sorted(bpl_programs), 4)

The files are unchanged copies. The columns give our result for each program (logs/ULR_vs_UPL_logs.zip,
timeout 1,000 s per run): the verdict of each run and its wall clock. The 9 programs with a run
above 300 s are those that --subset, with its 300 s timeout, stops earlier than our run did.

